<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Trinidad and Tobago</h1><p class="st-meta">1889 CE – 1962 CE · capital Port of Spain</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British colony joining Trinidad and Tobago from 1889, transformed by oil, labour revolt, calypso and steelpan before independence in 1962.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> joined struggling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-trinidad">Colony of Trinidad</a> in 1889, and in 1899 Tobago became a ward of the combined colony, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a>. The union was administrative, and Tobagonians often felt neglected by the larger island.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> government left power with the governor and nominated officials. Commercial oil production began in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> in the 1900s, and asphalt from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitch-lake">Pitch Lake</a> was exported worldwide. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-cipriani">Arthur Cipriani</a> led a reform movement in the 1920s, and the 1937 oilfield strikes and riots, inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uriah-butler">Uriah Butler</a>, led to unions and reform. In 1941 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> built bases at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaguaramas">Chaguaramas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad-and-tobago-carnival">Carnival</a>, calypso and the steelpan flourished among a population of African and Indian descent.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">Universal suffrage</a> came in 1946. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-williams">Eric Williams</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-national-movement">People's National Movement</a> in 1956 and became chief minister. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a> hosted the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-indies-federation">West Indies Federation</a>, and after it collapsed the colony became independent as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trinidad-and-tobago">Trinidad and Tobago</a> on 31 August 1962.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1889 CE – 1962 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.29%;width:1.45%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1889 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port of Spain</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Arthur Cipriani, Uriah Butler, Eric Williams</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Hinduism, Anglicanism and Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Trinidadian Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/trinidad-and-tobago">Trinidad and Tobago</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Trinidad and Tobago</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=colony-of-trinidad-and-tobago" aria-label="Colony of Trinidad and Tobago on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2985 1780 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Trinidad and Tobago lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3305 2036L3305 2036M3305 2036L4997 651M3305 2036L3305 2036M3305 2036L3305 2036"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3305 2036h0M4997 651h0M3305 2036h0M3305 2036h0"/><path class="map-dot-ha